}=3$ are eigenvalues, and \n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nare the respective eigenvectors. Find the matrices $P$ and $D$ such that $PD{P}^{-1}=A,$ where $D$ is a diagonal matrix." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404273 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c42e4814-ec50-5416-8161-bbb51b0ed62b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404273 #edb/ref 1074 "Since the eigenvalues of the matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=1,$ ${\\lambda }_{2}=2,$ ${\\lambda }_{3}=3,$ we construct the diagonal matrix $D$ by writing the eigenvalues in the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, to construct the matrix $P,$ we simply write the respective eigenvectors as columns: \n\n- the $1$st column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{1}=1,$\n\n- the $2$nd column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{2}=2,$ and\n\n- the $3$rd column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{3}=3.$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404274 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404275 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404274 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404276 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404274 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404277 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404274 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404278 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404274 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404279 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404274 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404274 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404274 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186404278 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404274 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f8de3def-44e0-5291-9c5d-3c0a5037be6f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404275 #edb/ref 1080 "$D=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]$ and  $P=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404275 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404275 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cd8e2916-1175-544e-9d6d-7e8a9cd2eca1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404276 #edb/ref 1080 "$D=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]$ and  $P=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404276 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404276 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "812a013d-6c97-5c8d-8555-41c27f26371f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404277 #edb/ref 1080 "$D=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]$ and  $P=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404277 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404277 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "62777a5a-2c5b-5c2c-bc49-88fd1f72656d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404278 #edb/ref 1080 "$D=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]$ and  $P=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404278 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404278 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "58ff7c16-1b9d-5ada-98a5-763a6cfe2824" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404279 #edb/ref 1080 "$D=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ and  $P=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404279 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404279 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1184eb62-ac2c-5e6b-abd1-f1c4d51d39b0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404280 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186404281 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404280 #edb/ref 1069 "q-83854" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404280 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404280 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 6 & -1 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \nThe matrix $A$ has eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=1,$ ${\\lambda }_{2}=-1,$ and ${\\lambda }_{3}=2.$\nFind a diagonal matrix $D$ and an invertible matrix $P$ such that $A=PD{P}^{-1}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404280 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "303c15f5-3e83-55c0-a519-b60eaa51efba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404280 #edb/ref 1074 "We apply the diagonalization algorithm.\n\n**Step 1.**  Notice that we are already given the eigenvalues of the matrix: \n\n$\\,$ ${\\lambda }_{1}=1,\\,$ ${\\lambda }_{2}=-1,\\,$ ${\\lambda }_{3}=2.$ \n\n**Step 2.** Now, we need to find an eigenvector basis of $A.$ Applying our usual method, we find the following.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 6 & -2 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-I)x=0$ gives us the eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=-1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-(-1)I & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 6 & 0 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-(-1)I)x=0$ gives us the eigenvector ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{3}=2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-2I & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 6 & -3 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-2I)x=0$ gives us the eigenvector ${v}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 3.** We construct the diagonal matrix $D$ and the invertible matrix $P$ in the usual way, and this gives us the following:\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,P=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404281 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404282 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404281 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404283 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404281 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404284 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404281 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404285 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404281 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404286 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404281 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404281 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404281 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186404284 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404281 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e147ba3d-c970-55a9-ac96-8187378e9cae" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404282 #edb/ref 1080 "$D=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $P=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404282 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404282 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "91c8360c-3a50-5dde-b1bc-982c3982cc9e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404283 #edb/ref 1080 "$D=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $P=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404283 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404283 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f6699882-8461-5d24-9c25-bf00717bab1d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404284 #edb/ref 1080 "$D=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $P=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404284 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404284 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e9b4c43c-1866-559f-80a2-eb60