$D$ by writing the eigenvalues in the main diagonal: \n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, to construct the matrix $P,$ we simply write the respective eigenvectors as columns: \n\n- the $1$st column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{1}=-4,$\n\n- the $2$nd column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{2}=3,$ and\n\n- the $3$rd column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{3}=0.$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 13\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 13\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]{[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 13\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, we get $a=2,$ $b=13,$ and $c=3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404309 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404310 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404309 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404311 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404309 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404312 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404309 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404313 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404309 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404314 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404309 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404309 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404309 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186404312 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404309 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "8345e678-341d-5cbb-a53f-7923d2b2c4f1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404310 #edb/ref 1080 "$a=2,$ $b=3,$ and $c=13$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404310 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404310 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e82133f4-cf40-52df-89fc-b9095a2ed393" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404311 #edb/ref 1080 "$a=-2,$ $b=13,$ and $c=3$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1759